steps.bodyMd:
The **Run as** sheet asks *Who does the work?* and answers it in one line: *An agent brings its own skills, knowledge and connected apps.*

Four things travel with it into the run:

- its **instructions** — how it writes, what it must never do;
- its **skills** — the ways of working it was given;
- its **knowledge bases** — what it may look things up in;
- its **connected apps**.

And one thing stops being yours: the **model**. An agent runs on its own model, so an item with an agent is stored with tier **Auto** — the tier you left on the slider is not what runs, and **Edit** has no tier field at all. The first row of the sheet, **No agent**, is hinted *Runs as a plain prompt* — your sentence, your apps, your tier, nothing else.
